{%- comment -%}
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  CART DRAWER
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  The theme's native cart drawer, restyled to the BioPharma v2 design. This is a restyle: the markup below is new, but
  every element that `assets/theme.js` reaches for is the same element it was before, in the same place, so no cart
  behaviour changed and no JS selector had to move.

  THE HOOKS, and what breaks if one is renamed or re-nested:

    <cart-drawer id="cart-drawer">   `aria-controls="cart-drawer"` toggles open it. On every cart:change, CartDrawer
                                     re-fetches this section and does
                                     `.querySelector('cart-drawer').innerHTML` -> replaceChildren. That is why every
                                     figure below is Liquid: the drawer re-renders server-side, it never patches numbers
                                     in the DOM.
    slot="header" / slot="footer"    the shadow template's named slots. An empty slot hides its wrapper, so the header
                                     slot always gets an element. Everything unslotted lands in part="body", the one
                                     scrolling region.
    .cart-drawer__footer             theme.css keys the footer padding off it.
    .cart-drawer__order-note         theme.css dims the header and body while the note overlay is open.
    .drawer--center-body             CartDrawer toggles this class itself when the cart empties. The empty state here
                                     carries its own recommendations, so CWC_cart_drawer.css neutralises the centring
                                     rather than fighting the JS for the class.
    <free-shipping-bar>              FreeShippingBar writes its message into the element's FIRST <span>. The progress
                                     track is therefore a sibling of the element, not a child of it.
    <cart-note> / <cart-note-dialog> the note autosaves on change of [name="note"].
    form[action=routes.cart_url]     the checkout form. button[name="checkout"] is its submit.

    Line-level hooks live in `snippets/CWC_cart-line-item.liquid`, which documents them.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% style %}
  #cart-drawer {
    --cwc-cart-accent: {{ section.settings.accent_color | default: '#5BA90F' }};
    --cwc-cart-accent-deep: {{ section.settings.accent_deep_color | default: '#44681A' }};
    --cwc-cart-surface: {{ section.settings.surface_color | default: '#FFFFFF' }};
    --cwc-cart-surface-soft: {{ section.settings.surface_soft_color | default: '#F5F4F0' }};
    --cwc-cart-surface-recs: {{ section.settings.recs_bg_color | default: '#FAFAF8' }};
    --cwc-cart-ink: {{ section.settings.text_color | default: '#1F1F1C' }};

    /* Rules and muted text are the ink at a fixed opacity, so a darker or lighter
       ink carries them with it instead of leaving a mismatched grey behind. */
    --cwc-cart-line: rgba({{ section.settings.text_color.red | default: 31 }}, {{ section.settings.text_color.green | default: 31 }}, {{ section.settings.text_color.blue | default: 28 }}, 0.14);
    --cwc-cart-line-soft: rgba({{ section.settings.text_color.red | default: 31 }}, {{ section.settings.text_color.green | default: 31 }}, {{ section.settings.text_color.blue | default: 28 }}, 0.08);
    --cwc-cart-muted: rgba({{ section.settings.text_color.red | default: 31 }}, {{ section.settings.text_color.green | default: 31 }}, {{ section.settings.text_color.blue | default: 28 }}, 0.62);
    --cwc-cart-faint: rgba({{ section.settings.text_color.red | default: 31 }}, {{ section.settings.text_color.green | default: 31 }}, {{ section.settings.text_color.blue | default: 28 }}, 0.40);
    --cwc-cart-danger: {{ section.settings.remove_color | default: '#B03A2E' }};
  }
{% endstyle %}

{{ 'CWC_fonts.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'CWC_cart_drawer.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'CWC_cart_drawer.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- liquid
  comment
    RECOMMENDATIONS — two passes through this same Liquid.

    Pass 1 is the ordinary render (page load, or CartDrawer replacing its own
    children after a cart change). `recommendations.performed` is false, so the
    strip renders from the fallback list and <cwc-cart-recs> goes and fetches the
    real thing.

    Pass 2 is that fetch: /recommendations/products?product_id=..&intent=..&
    section_id=cart-drawer. Shopify re-renders this whole section with the
    `recommendations` object populated; the element lifts out just the track and
    swaps it in.

    Why not the theme's own <product-recommendations>: it resolves its section id
    with closest('.shopify-section'), and Drawer inherits shouldAppendToBody, so
    the moment this drawer is opened it is moved to <body> and that lookup
    returns null. The section id is passed down from Liquid instead.
  endcomment
  assign recs_dynamic = false
  if section.settings.recommendations_source == 'dynamic'
    assign recs_dynamic = true
  endif

  assign recs_limit = section.settings.recommendations_limit | default: 6

  comment
    The recommendation API keys off one product, so the cart has to nominate one.
    The highest-value line is the best proxy for what the order is actually about
    — a $150 kit says more about intent than the shaker bottle added beside it.
  endcomment
  assign recs_seed_id = ''
  assign recs_seed_value = 0

  for line_item in cart.items
    if line_item.final_line_price > recs_seed_value
      assign recs_seed_value = line_item.final_line_price
      assign recs_seed_id = line_item.product_id
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Source for THIS render. Pass 2 hands us recommendations.products; every other
    render falls back to the curated list, which is also what stands if the API
    returns nothing and what a shopper with no JS sees.
  endcomment
  if recommendations.performed and recommendations.products_count > 0
    assign recs_products = recommendations.products
  else
    assign recs_products = section.settings.cross_sell_products
  endif

  comment
    Same two filters the section has always applied, now covering API results as
    well: never suggest what is already in the cart, never suggest what cannot be
    bought. Counted first so an empty strip is never rendered at all.
  endcomment
  assign recs_count = 0

  for product in recs_products
    assign products_in_cart = cart.items | where: 'product_id', product.id

    if products_in_cart.size == 0 and product.available
      assign recs_count = recs_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    With an empty cart there is no line to seed from, so the dynamic path cannot
    run and the curated list is all there is.
  endcomment
  assign recs_can_fetch = false
  if recs_dynamic and recs_seed_id != blank
    assign recs_can_fetch = true
  endif

  comment
    Resolved here rather than inline in the markup below. A comparison operator
    inside a conditional that sits INSIDE an HTML open tag reads as the start of
    a new element to an HTML-aware parser, which then swallows the closing tag
    and leaves the conditional looking unclosed — that is what makes a formatter
    append a stray endif at the end of the file.

    Note the wording: no tag delimiters anywhere in this comment. A liquid tag
    body ends at its first close sequence, so writing one inside prose here
    terminates the whole preamble early and turns the rest of it into markup.
  endcomment
  assign recs_show_nav = false
  if recs_count > 1
    assign recs_show_nav = true
  endif

  if cart.empty?
    assign cross_sell_heading = section.settings.cross_sell_title_empty
  else
    assign cross_sell_heading = section.settings.cross_sell_title
  endif

  comment
    Progress for the shipping track. The <free-shipping-bar> element owns the
    message and already carries the same total on its own attributes; this is the
    fill width for the rail drawn beside it, recomputed server-side on every cart
    change like everything else in the drawer.
  endcomment
  assign shipping_eligible_total = 0

  for line_item in cart.items
    if line_item.requires_shipping
      assign shipping_eligible_total = shipping_eligible_total | plus: line_item.final_line_price
    endif
  endfor

  assign cart_level_discount_total = 0

  for discount_application in cart.cart_level_discount_applications
    assign cart_level_discount_total = cart_level_discount_total | plus: discount_application.total_allocated_amount
  endfor

  assign shipping_eligible_total = shipping_eligible_total | minus: cart_level_discount_total
  assign free_shipping_threshold = settings.cart_free_shipping_threshold | times: 100

  assign free_shipping_progress = 0
  assign free_shipping_reached = false

  if free_shipping_threshold > 0
    assign free_shipping_progress = shipping_eligible_total | times: 100.0 | divided_by: free_shipping_threshold | at_most: 100 | at_least: 0
  endif

  if shipping_eligible_total >= free_shipping_threshold
    assign free_shipping_reached = true
  endif
-%}

<cart-drawer
  id="cart-drawer"
  class="cart-drawer drawer cwc_cart {% if cart.empty? %}drawer--center-body{% endif %} color-scheme color-scheme--{{ section.settings.color_scheme.id }}"
  initial-focus="false"
  handle-editor-events
>
  <div class="cwc_cart__head" slot="header">
    <span class="cwc_cart__head-title">{{ 'cart.general.title' | t }}</span>

    {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
      <span class="cwc_cart__head-count">
        {{- cart.item_count }}
        {{ cart.item_count | pluralize: 'item', 'items' -}}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if cart.empty? -%}
    <div class="cwc_cart__empty">
      <span class="cwc_cart__empty-mark">
        {% comment %} {%- render 'icon' with 'shopping_bag', width: 19 -%} {% endcomment %}
        <svg
          width="19"
          height="19"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="1.6"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
        >
          <path d="M5 8h14l-1.2 11.2a2 2 0 01-2 1.8H8.2a2 2 0 01-2-1.8z"/><path d="M9 8V6a3 3 0 016 0v2"/>
        </svg>
      </span>

      <p class="cwc_cart__empty-title">{{ section.settings.empty_title | default: 'Nothing here yet' }}</p>

      {%- if section.settings.empty_text != blank -%}
        <p class="cwc_cart__empty-text">{{ section.settings.empty_text }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- capture empty_links -%}
        {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
          {%- assign label_key = 'empty_link_' | append: i | append: '_label' -%}
          {%- assign url_key = 'empty_link_' | append: i | append: '_url' -%}
          {%- assign link_label = section.settings[label_key] -%}
          {%- assign link_url = section.settings[url_key] -%}

          {%- if link_label != blank and link_url != blank -%}
            <a href="{{ link_url }}" class="cwc_cart__empty-link">{{ link_label }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- if empty_links != blank -%}
        <div class="cwc_cart__empty-links">{{ empty_links }}</div>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          With no links configured the drawer would be a dead end, so the theme's
          own close control stands in — it puts the shopper back where they were.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="cwc_cart__empty-links">
          <button type="button" class="cwc_cart__empty-link" is="dialog-close-button">
            {{- 'cart.general.continue_shopping' | t -}}
          </button>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    {%- if settings.cart_show_free_shipping_bar and cart.requires_shipping -%}
      <div class="cwc_cart__ship {% if free_shipping_reached %}cwc_cart__ship--reached{% endif %}">
        <div class="cwc_cart__ship-row">
          {%- comment -%}
            HOOK: <free-shipping-bar> replaces the text of its own first <span>.
            The status word beside it is Liquid, and the rail below is a sibling —
            neither is inside the element, so neither can be overwritten.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- render 'free-shipping-bar' -%}

          {%- if free_shipping_reached -%}
            <span class="cwc_cart__ship-state"
              >&#10003; {{ section.settings.shipping_applied_label | default: 'Applied' -}}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <div class="cwc_cart__ship-track">
          <i class="cwc_cart__ship-fill" style="width: {{ free_shipping_progress }}%"></i>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="cwc_cart__items">
      {%- for line_item in cart.items -%}
        {%- render 'CWC_cart-line-item', line_item: line_item -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Rendered whenever there is something to show OR something to fetch. An
    element with an empty track starts hidden and unhides itself once the fetch
    lands; if nothing ever lands, it removes itself.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if recs_count > 0 or recs_can_fetch -%}
    <cwc-cart-recs
      class="cwc_cart__recs"
      {% if recs_count == 0 %}hidden{% endif %}
      {%- if recs_can_fetch %}
        data-cwc-recs-section="{{ section.id }}"
        data-cwc-recs-product="{{ recs_seed_id }}"
        data-cwc-recs-limit="{{ recs_limit }}"
        {%- comment -%}
          Tried in order. "complementary" is the merchant's own pairing from the
          Search & Discovery app and is the better answer where it exists, but it
          returns nothing at all unless someone has configured it — so the
          algorithmic "related" stands behind it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        data-cwc-recs-intents="complementary,related"
      {%- endif %}
    >
      <div class="cwc_cart__recs-head">
        {%- if cross_sell_heading != blank -%}
          <p class="cwc_cart__recs-title">{{ cross_sell_heading }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The nav is rendered whenever a fetch could widen the strip past one
          card, and stays hidden until the card count justifies it — that count
          is not knowable server-side on the first pass.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="cwc_cart__recs-nav" data-cwc-recs-nav {% unless recs_show_nav %}hidden{% endunless %}>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="cwc_cart__recs-arrow"
            data-cwc-recs-prev
            aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.previous' | t | escape }}"
          >
            {%- render 'icon' with 'chevron-left', width: 9 -%}
          </button>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="cwc_cart__recs-arrow"
            data-cwc-recs-next
            aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.next' | t | escape }}"
          >
            {%- render 'icon' with 'chevron-right', width: 9 -%}
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cwc_cart__recs-track" data-cwc-recs-track>
        {%- assign recs_rendered = 0 -%}

        {%- for product in recs_products -%}
          {%- assign products_in_cart = cart.items | where: 'product_id', product.id -%}

          {%- if products_in_cart.size == 0 and product.available -%}
            {%- assign recs_rendered = recs_rendered | plus: 1 -%}

            {%- if recs_rendered > recs_limit -%}
              {%- break -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- render 'CWC_cart-rec-card', product: product, card_index: forloop.index -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </cwc-cart-recs>
  {%- endif -%}











    {%- unless cart.empty? -%}
      <form action="{{ routes.cart_url }}" method="POST" class="cart-drawer__footer cwc_cart__foot" slot="footer">
      {%- comment -%}
        These two clear the collection grid-mode cart attributes on submit. They
        are read by main-collection.liquid, and dropping them would strand a
        shopper's grid choice in the cart forever.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <input type="hidden" name="attributes[products_mobile_grid_mode]" value="">
      <input type="hidden" name="attributes[products_desktop_grid_mode]" value="">

      <div class="cwc_cart__totals">
        <div class="cwc_cart__total-row">
          <span>{{ 'cart.general.subtotal' | t }}</span>
          <span>
            {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
              {{- cart.original_total_price | money_with_currency -}}
            {%- else -%}
              {{- cart.original_total_price | money -}}
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          One savings row covering every discount the cart holds, line-level and
          cart-level alike — cart.total_discount is exactly that sum, so the three
          rows always reconcile. The named discounts are listed under it so a
          shopper can still see which code did what.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if cart.total_discount > 0 -%}
          <div class="cwc_cart__total-row cwc_cart__total-row--save">
            <span>{{ section.settings.savings_label | default: 'Savings' }}</span>
            <span>
              &minus;
              {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
                {{- cart.total_discount | money_with_currency -}}
              {%- else -%}
                {{- cart.total_discount | money -}}
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
          </div>

          {%- if cart.cart_level_discount_applications.size > 0 -%}
            <ul class="cwc_cart__discounts" role="list">
              {%- for discount_application in cart.cart_level_discount_applications -%}
                <li class="cwc_cart__discount">
                  {%- render 'icon' with 'discount', width: 11 -%}
                  {{ discount_application.title }}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if settings.cart_show_free_shipping_bar and cart.requires_shipping and free_shipping_reached -%}
          <div class="cwc_cart__total-row">
            <span>{{ section.settings.shipping_row_label | default: 'Shipping' }}</span>
            <span>{{ section.settings.shipping_free_label | default: 'Free' }}</span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="cwc_cart__total-row cwc_cart__total-row--grand">
          <span>{{ 'cart.general.total' | t }}</span>
          <span class="cwc_cart__total-value">
            {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
              {{- cart.total_price | money_with_currency -}}
            {%- else -%}
              {{- cart.total_price | money -}}
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </div>

        {%- if section.settings.show_shipping_text -%}
          <p class="cwc_cart__foot-note">{{ 'cart.general.taxes_and_shipping_at_checkout' | t }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.show_cart_note -%}
          {%- assign cart_note_dialog_id = 'cart-note-' | append: section.id -%}

          <button type="button" class="cwc_cart__note-toggle" aria-controls="{{ cart_note_dialog_id }}">
            {%- if cart.note != blank -%}
              {{- 'cart.general.edit_order_note' | t -}}
            {%- else -%}
              {{- 'cart.general.add_order_note' | t -}}
            {%- endif -%}
          </button>

          <cart-note-dialog id="{{ cart_note_dialog_id }}" class="cart-drawer__order-note cwc_cart__note">
            <div class="form">
              <cart-note class="form-control">
                {%- assign order_note = 'cart.general.order_note' | t -%}
                {%- assign placeholder = 'cart.general.note_placeholder' | t -%}
                {%- render 'input',
                  name: 'note',
                  multiline: 3,
                  label: order_note,
                  value: cart.note,
                  placeholder: placeholder,
                  show_label_as_block: true
                -%}
              </cart-note>

              <button type="button" class="button" is="dialog-close-button">{{ 'cart.general.save_note' | t }}</button>
            </div>
          </cart-note-dialog>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="cwc_cart__actions">
          {%- if section.settings.show_checkout_button -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              HOOK: name="checkout" on a submit inside the form posting to
              routes.cart_url. That pair is the checkout, nothing else.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <button type="submit" name="checkout" class="cwc_cart__checkout">
              {% comment %} {{- 'cart.general.checkout' | t -}} {% endcomment %}
              Secure Checkout

              {%- if section.settings.show_price_in_checkout_button -%}
                <span class="cwc_cart__checkout-price">
                  {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
                    {{- cart.total_price | money_with_currency -}}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {{- cart.total_price | money -}}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </button>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.show_view_cart_button or section.settings.show_checkout_button == false -%}
            <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" class="cwc_cart__view-cart">{{ 'cart.general.view_cart' | t }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            "Continue shopping" closes the drawer instead of navigating — the
            shopper is already on the page they wanted. is="dialog-close-button"
            is the theme's own close control.
          {%- endcomment -%}

          {% comment %}
            <button type="button" class="cwc_cart__continue" is="dialog-close-button">
              {{- section.settings.continue_label | default: 'Continue shopping' -}}
            </button>
          {% endcomment %}
        </div>

        {%- assign trust_marks = section.settings.trust_marks | split: ',' -%}

        {%- if trust_marks.size > 0 -%}
          <ul class="cwc_cart__marks" role="list">
            {%- for mark in trust_marks -%}
              {%- if mark != blank -%}
                <li class="cwc_cart__mark">{{ mark | strip }}</li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      </form>
    {%- endunless -%}
    </cart-drawer>

    {% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.cart_drawer.name",
  "class": "shopify-section--cart-drawer",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.cart_drawer.page_info"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.cart_drawer.free_shipping_bar_info"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:global.colors.scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_cart_note",
      "label": "t:sections.cart_drawer.show_cart_note",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_shipping_text",
      "label": "t:sections.cart_drawer.show_shipping_text",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_view_cart_button",
      "label": "t:sections.cart_drawer.show_view_cart_button",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_checkout_button",
      "label": "t:sections.cart_drawer.show_checkout_button",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_price_in_checkout_button",
      "label": "t:sections.cart_drawer.show_price_in_checkout_button",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Colors"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent_color",
      "label": "Accent",
      "info": "Checkout button, progress bar, subscription badge.",
      "default": "#5BA90F"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent_deep_color",
      "label": "Accent (deep)",
      "info": "Savings text and badge labels.",
      "default": "#44681A"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Text",
      "info": "Rules and muted text derive from this color.",
      "default": "#1F1F1C"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "surface_color",
      "label": "Drawer background",
      "default": "#FFFFFF"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "surface_soft_color",
      "label": "Shipping bar background",
      "default": "#F5F4F0"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "recs_bg_color",
      "label": "Recommendations background",
      "default": "#FAFAF8"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "remove_color",
      "label": "Remove (hover)",
      "default": "#B03A2E"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Footer"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "savings_label",
      "label": "Savings row label",
      "info": "Shown when the cart holds any discount. The amount is the cart's own total discount.",
      "default": "Bundle & subscription savings"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "shipping_row_label",
      "label": "Shipping row label",
      "default": "Shipping"
    },
    {
